Build a generic finite state machine in TypeScript with state transitions and gu
Write `state_machine.ts` (ESM, TypeScript 5.x, no external deps) implementing a generic finite state machine.

## Interface
```typescript
export class StateMachine<S extends string, E extends string> {
  constructor(states: Record<S, StateConfig<S, E>>, initialState: S, options?: StateMachineOptions);
  getState(): S;
  send(event: E): boolean;
}
```

On successful transition: currentState.onExit → transition.action → newState.onEnter.
On rejected transition (no definition or guard fails): return false, no side effects.

