Build a PubSub class with wildcard pattern subscription and publish/subscribe me
Write `pubsub.ts` (or `pubsub.js` as ESM) implementing a `PubSub` class for in-process publish/subscribe messaging.

## Interface
```typescript
type Handler = (topic: string, message: unknown) => void;

class PubSub {
  subscribe(pattern: string, handler: Handler): () => void;
  // Returns an unsubscribe function.
  // Pattern can be:
  //   - exact: "user.created"
  //   - single-level wildcard: "user.*" matches "user.created", "user.deleted" but NOT "user.x.y"
  //   - multi-level wildcard: "user.#" matches "user.created", "user.profile.updated", etc.

  publish(topic: string, message: unknown): number;
  // Publish message to topic. Returns number of handlers called.

  subscriberCount(pattern: string): number;
  // Returns number of active subscriptions for this exact pattern string.
}
```

## Wildcard rules
- `*` matches exactly one topic segment (segments split by `.`)
- `#` matches zero or more segments at the end
- `user.*` matches `user.login` but not `user.login.success`
- `user.#` matches `user.login`, `user.login.success`, `user` (zero segments)
- Patterns without wildcards must match exactly

